  "rule": "a state whose ONLY inter-arm difference is a `timeout` on the SECOND arm, while the arms ran in the frozen sequential order under the shared per-state allowance, is classified as ORDER_ATTRIBUTABLE.  Its V2 difference is reported but may NOT be read as a scorer mechanism advantage: the second arm was charged for time it did not spend.  A `timeout` on the FIRST arm is never order-attributable.  Every affected state keeps its record and stays in the 64-state denominator; none is dropped, replaced or re-run.",
  "v1_is_order_invariant": "V1 compares the FIRST step, and no scorer call happens before it, so the second arm has spent nothing and no deadline can have fired.  V1 therefore cannot be order-sensitive and no V2 order effect can reach it.",
